A||N||6||jron||Swaying rearend.||||1||
Z||000000||jron||12-30-2001||08:46 AM|||| I just got my 85GT 2.8 rebuild running,first time at this. When I drive down the road,slow 5-10mpr. the rear end sways real bad. I have checked all that I can find and everything seems tight. I know that it needs an alignment but will that cause it to sway at low speeds ?? Sure could use some expert help on this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||08:52 AM||||It may be the alignment if they didn't line everything up correctly when they bolted the cradle back in. There are 2 bolts that hook the strut to the hub. They should have marked it when they removed it so they could get it lined up close. If you look at the wheel you should see it tilted out or in top to bottom if this is wrong. I have also seen the rear bearings gone and making a sway. You can jack that wheel up and shake it to see if there is any play.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||08:53 AM||||Oh By The way Welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000003||Mickey_Moose||12-30-2001||11:45 AM||||...also check the rear struts and strut mounts...worn struts or broken top mounts also cause the rear end to sway<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||12-30-2001||11:45 AM||||Welcome to the forum. When I rebuilt my engine and put it back in, the car wandered like a drunken sailor at all speeds till it was aligned. Get it aligned and this should solve your problem, unless, like stated above you have something else worn out.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||blakeinspace||12-31-2001||01:43 PM||||welcome from another new inductee...<P>My FORM did much the same, but was REALLY hairraising at speed.  Back end would squat down and shift over with a slight bit of throttle and when gas was let off, the car sat up and shifted back the other way... Put a new meaning in "We drive excitement"  A new dog bone helped but did not eliminate swaying.<BR>Traced my problem to VERY worn bushings on passenges side radius bar (lateral bar).  I replaced all bushings with poly.  For some reason other side was not near as worn.  But that solved my trouble.... Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||12-31-2001||05:53 PM||||Sounds like alignment.  Either just out of alignment or because of worn suspension parts shifting.  Start with the alignemnt.  A good shop should warn you if they find worn suspension parts.||||reg||1
